# Copy this file to .env. It is gitignored - never commit the filled-in
# version, and never paste it into a chat or an issue.
#
# The defaults below are for a database on your own machine, which is what
# everyone develops and tests against.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database - your own MySQL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# XAMPP's default is user root with no password. Start MySQL from the XAMPP
# control panel first, then:
#
#     npm run db:setup     create the schema (needs plant_registry_schema.sql)
#     npm run db:seed      load the demo dataset
#
# The server will not start without this. There is no in-memory fallback: a
# prototype quietly serving empty data that is never saved would be worse than
# one that says what is missing.

DATABASE_URL=mysql://root@127.0.0.1:3306/plant_registry

# Running the tests reseeds whichever database this points at, and refuses
# outright if it is not on this machine - the suites create and archive real
# records, and that is not litter to leave in a database anyone else is using.

# No TLS settings here: a local MySQL has no certificate and refuses the
# handshake outright, so the server does not attempt one. A hosted database
# needs MYSQL_SSL_CA_CERT set to its CA certificate; that is the only
# difference, and it is configuration rather than a code change.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public address
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Left blank the server uses this machine's network address, which is what the
# phone hand-off and a local demo want. Only set this when hosting.
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# IoT sensor readings (MQTT)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Left out, these default to the values below, which match
# iot-kit/FloraScan_Node. Change the sketch's MQTT_HOST and TOPIC_PREFIX
# to match if you change them here.
# MQTT_URL=mqtt://broker.hivemq.com:1883
# MQTT_TOPIC_PREFIX=florascan-swinburne-demo
